<div id="ops" class="visually-hidden" aria-hidden="true"></div>
<section id="fleet" class="hd-panel mb-4 hd-help-section">
    <h2 class="h5">Fleet</h2>
    <p class="text-secondary small mb-2"><strong>Purpose:</strong> Digital Technology console — computers, live util, sessions, online status, client version, cost, and stats in one place.</p>
    <ol class="small mb-0">
        <li>Open <a asp-page="/Fleet">Fleet</a>. Tabs load on demand (only the active tab’s data runs on first paint).</li>
        <li>Legacy URLs (<code>/</code>, <code>/Ops</code>, Sessions, Online Status, Client Version, Cost, Stats) redirect into the matching Fleet tab.</li>
        <li><strong>Live</strong> shows estate-wide 30s util gauges for every known machine (not Flood-gated).</li>
        <li>Online Status still uses on-demand Ping / Test RDP — probes are not run on every page load.</li>
    </ol>
</section>

<section id="fleet-live" class="hd-panel mb-4 hd-help-section">
    <h2 class="h5">Fleet → Live</h2>
    <p class="text-secondary small mb-2"><strong>Purpose:</strong> live CPU/GPU/RAM/disk/network for the whole estate — every machine with a Heimdall client.</p>
    <ol class="small mb-0">
        <li>Open <a asp-page="/Fleet" asp-route-tab="live">Fleet → Live</a>. Auto-refreshes every 30s.</li>
        <li>Sampling is always-on after the agent’s first heartbeat — no Flood enrollment required.</li>
        <li>Active / Idle badges apply while TUFLOW is detected on that host; most estate machines show gauges with Active/Idle as —.</li>
        <li>Flood’s own Live tab (under <a asp-page="/Flood">Flood hub</a>) stays scoped to the Flood allowlist.</li>
    </ol>
</section>

<section id="machines" class="hd-panel mb-4 hd-help-section">
    <h2 class="h5">Computers</h2>
    <p class="text-secondary small mb-2"><strong>Purpose:</strong> fleet list by team — status and utilisation at a glance (Fleet → All computers).</p>
    <ol class="small mb-0">
        <li>Computers are grouped under <strong>team section headings</strong>. Active app-list names for that team appear beside the heading.</li>
        <li>Summary counts (Computers / Active / Idle / Off) sit beside the Period control — Computers in gold; Active / Idle / Off labels in status colours (green / amber / red); silver numbers centered underneath. Click any column header to sort (first click descending, then toggle).</li>
        <li><strong>Status</strong> (5‑minute check-in): green Active = online with a non-disconnected session; amber Idle = online, no active session; red Off = no recent check-in. Status is colored text (same size as the computer name).</li>
        <li><strong>Period</strong> (Today / 24h / 5d / 7d / 30d / All) sets Active / Passive / Free % and GPU·CPU·IO columns for the whole list.</li>
        <li>Click any metric cell (Active, Passive, Free, GPU h, CPU h, Dr, Dw, NTx, NRx) to open a <strong>breakdown</strong> of processes, people, and days that built that total. Period cycling on cells was removed — change Period only via the dropdown.</li>
        <li>Active % is non-disconnected session time over the calendar window. Passive, GPU/CPU hours, and disk/network columns use <strong>always-on 30s fleet samples</strong> from every Heimdall client (independent of Flood enrollment). Until samples arrive those cells show —.</li>
        <li>Process names on hardware/Passive breakdowns require an <strong>updated agent</strong> that uploads top processes with each fleet sample. Older clients still contribute machine totals; the drill-down notes when process history is missing.</li>
        <li>Name links to computer detail. Assign teams and app lists under <a asp-page="/Teams">Applications → Teams</a>.</li>
        <li>Sessions live under <a asp-page="/Fleet" asp-route-tab="sessions">Fleet → Sessions</a>.</li>
    </ol>
</section>

<section id="applications" class="hd-panel mb-4 hd-help-section">
    <h2 class="h5">Application Usage</h2>
    <p class="text-secondary small mb-2"><strong>Purpose:</strong> fleet-wide usage for tracked processes — time, machines, users, and runs over the selected period.</p>
    <ol class="small mb-0">
        <li>Pick a <strong>Period</strong> and Apply. Columns: Users, Machines, Avg open, Runs, Total time, Last seen.</li>
        <li>Click a row for per-machine / per-user detail. Long names truncate; hover for the full title.</li>
        <li>To change <em>what</em> counts as an application (vs. Core Windows / SOE noise), use <a asp-page="/AppLists" asp-fragment="app-lists">App lists</a> or <a asp-page="/Discovery" asp-fragment="discovery">Discovery &amp; Classification</a>.</li>
    </ol>
</section>

<section id="app-lists" class="hd-panel mb-4 hd-help-section">
    <h2 class="h5">App lists</h2>
    <p class="text-secondary small mb-2">
        <strong>Purpose:</strong> the only place to build and apply lists of processes agents should track.
        Tabs (Fleet-style): <strong>Software Lists</strong>, <strong>Create</strong>, <strong>Analyze PC</strong>.
    </p>
    <ol class="small">
        <li><strong>Software Lists</strong> — browse/edit/export existing lists, plus <em>Track Software</em> (apply a list to Global / regions / offices / machines). Team apply/ignore also lives under <a asp-page="/Teams">Teams</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Create</strong> — compact Name / optional Team / Notes. Pick apps from the catalog table (Discovery-style) with <em>Add to list</em>, then <em>Save</em> (requires a name). Use <em>Add custom software to catalog</em> for path/exe/friendly name/description before the app is installed anywhere.</li>
        <li><strong>Analyze PC</strong> — machine lookup, inventory, team-apps hunting, bulk classification import/export.</li>
        <li>Agents only track processes that appear on an applied App list (plus any leftover legacy Tracking Config includes). There is no separate Known Apps track list.</li>
        <li><strong>Buttons</strong> — Gold = primary; Silver = secondary; Black = nav; Rose = cancel/remove.</li>
        <li><strong>Changelog</strong> opens the full <a asp-page="/AppListChangelog">App list changelog</a>.</li>
    </ol>
</section>

<section id="app-list-changelog" class="hd-panel mb-4 hd-help-section">
    <h2 class="h5">App list changelog</h2>
    <p class="text-secondary small mb-2"><strong>Purpose:</strong> full audit trail for app-list work — list create/edit, uploads, assignments, machine analysis approvals, and classification imports.</p>
    <ol class="small mb-0">
        <li>Open from <em>View Changelog</em> on <a asp-page="/AppLists" asp-fragment="app-lists">App lists</a> (or go directly to <a asp-page="/AppListChangelog">/AppListChangelog</a>).</li>
        <li>Newest entries first; 50 rows per page with Previous / Next when needed.</li>
        <li>Click column headers to sort within the current page.</li>
    </ol>
</section>

<section id="discovery" class="hd-panel mb-4 hd-help-section">
    <h2 class="h5">Discovery &amp; Classification</h2>
    <p class="text-secondary small mb-2">
        <strong>Purpose:</strong> classify processes into Core Windows / SOE / Specialization. By default only unclassified apps
        and pending suggestions (from CSV import or heuristics) are listed.
    </p>
    <ol class="small mb-0">
        <li><strong>Name &amp; Location</strong> — process name (double-click to rename) and read-only path underneath. Click <em>Name</em> or <em>Location</em> in the header to sort (no arrow indicators). Drag column borders to resize; widths persist for the browser session.</li>
        <li><strong>Version</strong> — file/product/manual/path-derived value (no source subtitle).</li>
        <li><strong>Category</strong> / <strong>Subcategory</strong> — from CSV import or Edit/Save; shown when present (not always “—”).</li>
        <li><strong>Classification</strong> — in-row dropdown (Core Windows / SOE / Specialization). Click <strong>Set</strong> to apply that group (and current Category/Subcategory).</li>
        <li><strong>Installs</strong> — machines that reported the process; hover for the host list.</li>
        <li><strong>Approve</strong> (gold) — commits a pending Group suggestion. <strong>Set</strong> uses the Classification dropdown instead of a modal.</li>
        <li><strong>Search</strong> — type a filter and press Search or Enter (not live-as-you-type).</li>
        <li><strong>Missing path</strong> — catalog rows with an empty ExecutablePath (shown as “missing path”). Use <strong>Find missing paths</strong> (or per-row <strong>Find path</strong>) to reuse paths from process samples / machine inventories; remaining gaps can trigger Request Inventory on those hosts. Or request inventory manually on App Lists.</li>
        <li><strong>Show classified</strong> — expand the list beyond unclassified / pending suggestions. <strong>Descriptions</strong> toggle shows description sub-rows.</li>
        <li>Import classifications from <a asp-page="/AppLists" asp-fragment="csv-classifications">App lists → Bulk Update</a>; they appear here as pending until Approve/Set.</li>
    </ol>
</section>

<section id="socratize" class="hd-panel mb-4 hd-help-section">
    <h2 class="h5">Socratize</h2>
    <p class="text-secondary small mb-2"><strong>Purpose:</strong> a one-machine cost-justification brief — probes sessions, local vs. RDP time, utilisation, apps, and team, then gives a verdict.</p>
    <ol class="small mb-0">
        <li>Pick (or search for) a machine.</li>
        <li>Review the generated brief — utilisation score, busy metrics, apps in use, and a keep/investigate/retire-style verdict.</li>
        <li>The verdict's thresholds come from <a asp-page="/Utilization" asp-fragment="utilization">Utilization criteria</a> — tune those if verdicts feel off.</li>
    </ol>
</section>

<section id="sessions" class="hd-panel mb-4 hd-help-section">
    <h2 class="h5">Sessions</h2>
    <p class="text-secondary small mb-2"><strong>Purpose:</strong> logon / usage sessions — who signed in, local vs RDP, start/end, active vs disconnected time.</p>
    <ol class="small mb-0">
        <li>Under nav <strong>Machines → Sessions</strong>. Pick a period, then click a machine name (or multi-select) to open the session log.</li>
        <li>Each row shows user, Local / Inbound RDP, started, ended, total duration, active time, and disconnected time.</li>
        <li>Open-count buttons show who is on a machine right now; <em>Machine detail</em> links to the apps/metrics page for that host.</li>
    </ol>
</section>

<section id="remote-machines" class="hd-panel mb-4 hd-help-section">
    <h2 class="h5">Online Status</h2>
    <p class="text-secondary small mb-2"><strong>Purpose:</strong> RDP/RDS health — also under <a asp-page="/Fleet" asp-route-tab="online">Fleet → Online status</a>.</p>
    <ol class="small mb-0">
        <li>Review per-machine RDP health, ping, and Terminal Services status (refreshed by the agent, plus on-demand from the API server).</li>
        <li>Use <em>Connect</em> to download a small <code>.rdp</code> file for that hostname (opens with Windows Remote Desktop / mstsc). Browsers cannot run <code>mstsc /v:</code> directly.</li>
        <li>Use <em>Restart RDS</em> to queue a remote restart command for the agent to pick up; progress shows inline.</li>
    </ol>
</section>

<section id="tuflow-runs" class="hd-panel mb-4 hd-help-section">
    <h2 class="h5">TUFLOW Runs</h2>
    <p class="text-secondary small mb-2">
        <strong>Purpose:</strong> queue a TUFLOW start or graceful stop on Flood-enrolled machines.
        Nav under <strong>Flood</strong> (visible only to <code>Heimdall:StaffAccess:AdminEmails</code> ∪ <code>Heimdall:FloodTeamEmails</code>).
    </p>
    <ol class="small">
        <li>Enroll the modelling host on <strong>Flood → Enrollment</strong> first (Flood allowlist — not required for util sampling).</li>
        <li>On <strong>TUFLOW Runs</strong>, enter exe path, <code>.tcf</code>, optional scenarios/events/run name, then Start. The agent picks up within ~20s.</li>
        <li><strong>Stop gracefully</strong> asks the launcher to send a process-group break so TUFLOW can finish the current checkpoint (resume-friendly if your <code>.tcf</code> writes restart files — see <code>tuflow-automation/tcf/</code>).</li>
        <li>Progress comes from TUFLOW’s own <code>.tsf</code>; crashes from <code>.tlf</code> ERROR lines. Machine detail also shows a TUFLOW panel + recent run history for flood-gated users.</li>
        <li>Agent needs <code>%ProgramFiles%\Heimdall\Agent\TuflowLauncher\TuflowLauncher.exe</code> (included when you pack/install the client or run <code>Install-Agent</code>).</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="text-secondary small mb-0">
        POC uses free-form paths (not allowlisted batches yet). Modelling+DT RBAC is a follow-up.
    </p>
</section>

<section id="historical-dashboard" class="hd-panel mb-4 hd-help-section">
    <h2 class="h5">Flood hub (Historical + Sims)</h2>
    <p class="text-secondary small mb-2">
        <strong>Purpose:</strong> Flood-gated workspace — Live / Historical analytics for the Flood allowlist, Fleet Sims progress, and Enrollment.
        Open <a asp-page="/Flood">Flood</a> (visible only to <code>Heimdall:StaffAccess:AdminEmails</code> ∪ <code>Heimdall:FloodTeamEmails</code>).
        Legacy <code>/HistoricalDashboard</code> and <code>/FleetSimProgress</code> URLs redirect into this hub.
    </p>
    <ol class="small">
        <li><strong>Enrollment</strong> — Flood allowlist for TUFLOW Runs / sims. Search by hostname or last-known IP. Util sampling does <em>not</em> require enrollment (always-on for all clients).</li>
        <li><strong>Live</strong> — current CPU/GPU/RAM/disk/network from the latest snapshot on enrolled Flood machines, TUFLOW status (Active / Idle / Not Running), today’s runtime/active/GPU hours. Auto-refreshes every 30s. Estate-wide live util lives under <a asp-page="/Fleet" asp-route-tab="live">Fleet → Live</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Active vs Idle</strong> — while TUFLOW is running: Active if <em>TUFLOW process</em> GPU &gt; 5%, CPU &gt; 10%, or disk read/write &gt; 5 MB/s; otherwise Idle. Not Running when TUFLOW is not detected. Live gauges still show system-wide util.</li>
        <li><strong>Historical</strong> — fleet summary cards for enrolled machines, Totals (today / week / month / 30d / 3m / 6m / year) or Averages (daily / 7-day / monthly / all-time), plus rankings (GPU, CPU, RAM, disk I/O, most active).</li>
        <li><strong>Fleet Sims</strong> — active TUFLOW runs across Flood-enrolled machines (progress, elapsed, process/machine averages).</li>
        <li><strong>Machine detail</strong> — click a hostname for period summary cards and Chart.js time series (24h / 7d / 30d / 90d / 365d).</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="text-secondary small mb-0">
        <strong>Retention:</strong> raw 30s samples are purged after ~90 days by default (<code>Heimdall:FleetSnapshotRetention</code>).
        Rough disk estimate: about <em>N × 2,880</em> rows per day (N = sampling machines), so 10 hosts ≈ 28.8k rows/day.
        Derived metrics use Σ (util%/100)×Δt for GPU/CPU hours, Σ (RAM GB)×Δt for GB-hours, and Σ (MB/s × Δt)/1024 for transfer GB.
    </p>
</section>

<section id="staff-access" class="hd-panel mb-4 hd-help-section">
    <h2 class="h5">Staff RDP</h2>
    <p class="text-secondary small mb-2"><strong>Purpose:</strong> public-team machine pool — book up to 24 hours and Connect via an <code>.rdp</code> file (opens mstsc).</p>
    <ol class="small mb-0">
        <li>Sign in with your Windows/AD identity (Negotiate). The pool shows machines whose team is marked <strong>public-facing</strong> under Applications → Teams.</li>
        <li>If you belong to a Remote Access Group, the pool is further limited to those hosts; if you have no RAG membership, you see all public-facing machines.</li>
        <li><strong>Active User</strong> (green) means an Active session is present — you can still book (warning) and Connect (break-glass).</li>
        <li><strong>Book</strong> rejects overlapping bookings; cancel your own booking (admins can cancel any). Duration: 1h / 2h / 4h / 8h / end-of-day / 24h.</li>
        <li><strong>Connect</strong> downloads/opens a tiny <code>.rdp</code> file — browsers cannot launch <code>mstsc</code> directly; use Open with Remote Desktop.</li>
        <li>Live CPU/GPU metrics remain on the per-group Staff page linked as “Live metrics” when you have RAG membership.</li>
    </ol>
</section>

<section id="remote-access-groups" class="hd-panel mb-4 hd-help-section">
    <h2 class="h5">Remote Access Groups</h2>
    <p class="text-secondary small mb-2"><strong>Purpose:</strong> admin setup for <a asp-page="/StaffAccess" asp-fragment="staff-access">Staff Access</a> — who can see which machines, and which processes they can favourite.</p>
    <ol class="small mb-0">
        <li>Create a group, add staff by email (must match their Windows UPN or <code>user@domain</code> login).</li>
        <li>Assign machines to the group — only those machines are visible to its members.</li>
        <li>Optionally curate a favourite-process shortlist and toggle "favourites only" mode for the group.</li>
    </ol>
</section>

<section id="tracking-config" class="hd-panel mb-4 hd-help-section">
    <h2 class="h5">Tracking config</h2>
    <p class="text-secondary small mb-2"><strong>Purpose:</strong> sampling intervals, exclude lists, pauses, and metric thresholds for agents. What to <em>track</em> is owned by <a asp-page="/AppLists">App lists</a>.</p>
    <ol class="small mb-0">
        <li>Configs are scoped (All / Region / Office / Group / Machine) with priority — more specific scopes win.</li>
        <li>Exclude lists and pauses still live here. Prefer App lists (Create → Save → Apply) for includes. Legacy Tracking Config include JSON may still apply until cleared.</li>
        <li>Sample/upload/refresh intervals control agent chattiness — raise them on constrained networks.</li>
        <li>See <a asp-page="/Utilization" asp-fragment="utilization">Utilization criteria</a> for the scoring weights that consume this data.</li>
    </ol>
</section>

<section id="auth" class="hd-panel mb-4 hd-help-section">
    <h2 class="h5">Auth</h2>
    <p class="text-secondary small mb-2"><strong>Purpose:</strong> turn team-membership sources on/off under <strong>Admin → Auth</strong>. Not site-wide SSO.</p>
    <ol class="small mb-0">
        <li><strong>Manual / CSV</strong> (default on) — backup while Entra permissions are pending. Add people on team detail or <a asp-page="/Teams/ImportCsv">Import CSV</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Entra Graph sync</strong> (default off) — enable after DPAPI secrets are installed and Graph admin consent is granted. Use <em>Test Entra connection</em> on Auth: token OK + group-read fail usually means consent is still missing.</li>
        <li>At least one source stays enabled. Sync from Entra is blocked while the Entra toggle is off.</li>
    </ol>
</section>

<section id="teams" class="hd-panel mb-4 hd-help-section">
    <h2 class="h5">Teams</h2>
    <p class="text-secondary small mb-2"><strong>Purpose:</strong> org teams for Fleet machine sections, people, app lists, and Staff RDP visibility. Under <strong>Applications → Teams</strong>.</p>
    <ol class="small mb-0">
        <li>The list shows each team’s people, machines, and tracking / ignored app-list counts. Use <strong>Add team</strong> or <strong>Import CSV</strong>; open a row for detail.</li>
        <li>On <strong>Edit team</strong>, set name, code, parent, and <strong>Public-facing</strong> (machines appear in the Staff RDP pool — do not mark Flood/TUFLOW teams public).</li>
        <li>
            <strong>Entra membership</strong> — enable under <a asp-page="/Auth">Admin → Auth</a> when ready.
            On the API host run <code>scripts\Protect-HeimdallEntraSecret.ps1</code>
            (DPAPI file at <code>%ProgramData%\Heimdall\secrets\entra.json</code>).
            Never put <code>ClientSecret</code> in git or <code>appsettings.json</code>.
            App registration needs Application permissions <code>Group.Read.All</code> and <code>User.Read.All</code> (or <code>GroupMember.Read.All</code>) with admin consent; no redirect URI.
            On Edit team, paste the Entra group <strong>Object ID</strong>; on team detail use <em>Sync from Entra</em>
            (username from on-prem SAM when present, else UPN/mail local-part; optional <code>DefaultNetBiosDomain</code>).
        </li>
        <li><strong>Membership</strong> — add/edit/remove people (<code>firstname.lastname</code>); assign or unassign machines (never deletes a machine from the database). Manual people on an Entra-linked team are replaced on the next sync.</li>
        <li><strong>App lists</strong> — link lists as Tracking or Do not track for the whole team; use <strong>Machine overrides</strong> to force track or ignore a list on one host (override wins).</li>
        <li>CSV import supports <code>Username,Team</code> or full columns including <code>ParentTeam</code> and optional <code>Code</code>. Catalog editing stays on <a asp-page="/AppLists">App lists</a>.</li>
    </ol>
</section>

<section id="utilization" class="hd-panel mb-4 hd-help-section">
    <h2 class="h5">Utilization criteria</h2>
    <p class="text-secondary small mb-2"><strong>Purpose:</strong> the global weights and targets that produce the <a asp-page="/Socratize" asp-fragment="socratize">Socratize</a> verdict (and utilisation scoring elsewhere).</p>
    <ol class="small mb-0">
        <li>Weights (users, daily utilisation, busy metrics, app value) must add to 100% — the page shows a running total.</li>
        <li>Ideal targets (min users, ideal daily %, working hours/day) define what "good" looks like before scoring kicks in.</li>
        <li>High/Adequate/Mixed thresholds decide which verdict bucket a machine lands in.</li>
    </ol>
</section>

<section id="cost" class="hd-panel mb-4 hd-help-section">
    <h2 class="h5">Cost</h2>
    <p class="text-secondary small mb-2"><strong>Purpose:</strong> hardware purchase cost, warranty, support hours, and inventory/reimage identity — under <a asp-page="/Fleet" asp-route-tab="cost">Fleet → Cost</a>.</p>
    <ol class="small mb-0">
        <li>Edit a row to record purchase cost/currency, warranty dates, and hardware specs (or let the agent auto-fill what it can detect).</li>
        <li>Support hourly rate feeds into the <a asp-page="/Socratize" asp-fragment="socratize">Socratize</a> brief's cost-per-hour comparison.</li>
        <li>Reimage identity fields help distinguish a genuinely new machine from the same box after a reimage.</li>
    </ol>
</section>

<section id="stats" class="hd-panel mb-4 hd-help-section">
    <h2 class="h5">Stats</h2>
    <p class="text-secondary small mb-2"><strong>Purpose:</strong> usage analytics by machine scope — under <a asp-page="/Fleet" asp-route-tab="stats">Fleet → Stats</a>.</p>
    <ol class="small mb-0">
        <li>Pick a scope tab and date range; tables cover utilisation, app usage, and session counts for that scope.</li>
        <li>Click column headers to sort; use the filter box to narrow rows by name.</li>
    </ol>
</section>

<section id="client-version" class="hd-panel mb-4 hd-help-section">
    <h2 class="h5">Client Version</h2>
    <p class="text-secondary small mb-2"><strong>Purpose:</strong> under <strong>Machines</strong> — agent build vs. published version, online / in use / <strong>Active User</strong> (green = Active, red = Disconnected), and silent <strong>Deploy Client</strong> when the pack on this API host matches source.</p>
    <ol class="small mb-0">
        <li>On load the page checks source vs pack fingerprints; <strong>Deploy Client</strong> stays locked until the pack is Ready. <strong>Pack client</strong> always rebuilds and bumps version (N+1), even when already Ready (requires <code>Heimdall:RepoRoot</code> on D8R).</li>
        <li>Deploy queues a silent agent self-update (download + service restart only). Updates defer while any interactive session is Active — no logoff or reboot. Agents below version <code>3</code> do not support <code>UpdateClient</code> — Deploy marks them Failed with bootstrap guidance.</li>
        <li><strong>Bootstrap once:</strong> first upgrade from pre-3 / legacy clients needs Launch Control push or <code>Install.lnk</code> from the pack. After that, silent Deploy works for subsequent versions.</li>
        <li>Legacy SemVer builds count as version <code>1</code>; current packs use simple integers (baseline <code>3</code> = first UpdateClient-capable). Old <code>/Clients</code> URLs redirect here.</li>
    </ol>
</section>

<section id="admin-preferences" class="hd-panel mb-4 hd-help-section">
    <h2 class="h5">Admin menu: Theme &amp; database mode</h2>
    <p class="text-secondary small mb-2"><strong>Purpose:</strong> personal display preferences and the sandbox/live data toggle, both in the top-right <strong>Admin</strong> menu.</p>
    <ol class="small mb-0">
        <li><strong>Theme</strong> — the Admin menu links to the <a asp-page="/Theme">Theme page</a>, which offers premade looks (Original Recipe, Cosmic, Dark Slate, Light Clean) plus a full colour/font editor for building and saving your own named themes. The active theme is remembered via cookie.</li>
        <li><strong>Database mode</strong> — <em>Live</em> shows real agent data; <em>Sandbox (DEV)</em> is an isolated demo/test database. Agent ingest always writes to Live regardless of which mode you're browsing — don't confuse a quiet Sandbox view with agents being down.</li>
        <li>A <span class="hd-dev-badge" style="font-size:0.7rem;padding:0.1rem 0.4rem;">DEV</span>-style badge in the header means you're currently viewing the sandbox, not production data.</li>
    </ol>
</section>
